Fillets: the roundings of both edges of a face exactly as wide as the two,
which take the face away, their contacts along each other (mitcad#343).

The case: windows in a ring wall 3 thick (radii 112 and 115), each
window's floor and ceiling rounded with 1.5 on both edges, ending at the
pillars' full-rounded ends; the windows are a circular pattern's copies.
Both roundings are halves of one torus (113.5, 1.5), and their contacts on
the floor lie along each other at the wall's middle, ending at one point
on the floor's arc with the pillar's end. The bodies stored in the files
have the torus and no floor.

- ChFi3d_StripeEdgeInter: two stripes whose contacts on a common face
  overlap all along their ranges (one segment covering both, within a
  hundredth of each range) do not clash: they meet along their contacts.
  Before, OCCT took them for roundings too big for the face and failed
  ("fillets have too big radiuses").
- ChFi3d_Builder::Compute (joinEndsAlongContacts, after the stripes are in
  the data structure): for two stripes of one piece each whose contacts on
  a face lie along each other within ten times the approximation tolerance,
  the points their corners made where the contacts end on an edge of that
  face are made one, and that edge leaves the face on both sides of them
  (EXTERNAL); where both ends are joined, the second stripe's contact edge
  is replaced by the first's (its curve on the second blend projected
  anew, its transition turned where the curves run opposite ways), and the
  face has that edge on both sides. Before, each corner made its own point
  and each stripe its own contact edge: the face came out as a sliver of no
  area between them, or with the arc's pieces left on it and on the face
  at the end (an invalid result), depending on the copy of the window.

On the design's body before the item, the rounding of the four windows'
floors and ceilings (48 edges): valid, every face on the stored body's
within 1e-6 mm both ways, the change of volume -243.0297 against the
file's -243.0189 mm3; before, two of the four windows failed. Synthetic:
five windows with pillar ends in halves, both sills rounded with OCCT's
fillet alone: valid, the material taken within 2e-3 mm3 of the integral
over the sills' outlines; before, the fillet failed.

Upstream: new.
